  "method": "Three alternating fresh untraced processes and one MallocStackLogging full-history graph per version. Sigils owner thread polled non-blockingly with monotonic deadline; NimKit main work deliberately not drained. Trace uses leaks --fullStackHistory --outputGraph at checkpoint and malloc_history -highWaterMark -callTree plus live call tree.",
  "platform": "macOS 15.7.9 arm64, Nim 2.4.0, classic nim c -d:release --mm:arc, same Atlas dependencies and nim.cfg",
  "limitations": [
    "The sampled structure-only checkpoint isolates UI map retention, not complete view/layout or released-worker memory. Worker still owns pending code sources in both variants.",
    "Each allocation trace is one process; stack logging changes allocation timing and omits some no-stack allocations. Three untraced samples estimate variability.",
    "131,072 code lines produce substantial parser allocation traffic; cumulative totals here are not a claim that parser churn was fixed.",
    "RSS is process memory, not live object memory.",
    "Units on traced fields are preserved exactly as malloc_history prints them."
  ],
